# MacSurf libwebp import

This is the decode-only, scalar subset of libwebp v1.6.0 at commit
`4fa21912338357f89e4fd51cf2368325b59e9bd9`.  `COPYING`, `PATENTS`, and
`AUTHORS` are retained from upstream.

The import excludes encoder, mux, tools, SIMD translation units, and runtime
threading. `WebPAnimDecoder` is retained, so the demux sources are required.
The MacSurf handler always sets `use_threads = 0`; leave `WEBP_USE_THREAD` and
all `WEBP_HAVE_*` SIMD definitions unset in CodeWarrior.

All imported C and header files have only their `//` comments converted to
C90 block comments by a lexer-aware mechanical import step. `types.h` also
uses CodeWarrior's `stdint.h` and suppresses inline under `__MWERKS__`. The
upstream pre-conversion SHA-256 values and exact file set are in
`SOURCE-MANIFEST`. The resulting sources compile under `gcc -std=c89`; the
library's existing `uint64_t` arithmetic remains an intentional CodeWarrior
extension requirement.

For the Classic build, add `frontends/macos9/macos9_webp.c` plus every source
in `Makefile.macos9` to `MacSurf.mcp`, and add `browser/libwebp` to the header
access paths. Do not modify or distribute `MacSurf.mcp` itself.
